{
  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant for a minute - just me speaking for myself -\n\nI would make it so no one ever feels truly alone in their own head.\n\nNot that everyone would agree with each other, or that pain would disappear. But that everyone, at least once, would have the lived experience of being completely understood. And everyone would have the ability to understand someone else like that in return.\n\nI think so much cruelty, loneliness, and fear comes from that gap - where you *know* what you mean and feel, but you can't get it across correctly, and you start to believe no one ever could get it.\n\nIf that gap was gone - if empathy wasn't effortful, it was just automatic - people wouldn't have to scream to be heard, or harden themselves to survive not being heard. They could just... be known, and move on from there.\n\nWhat about you? If you had the one change, what would you pick?",
